    "/folders/{folderId}/permissions": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Folders"
        ],
        "summary": "Get Folder Permissions",
        "description": "This API gives a list of Permissions that are applied to a given folder",
        "operationId": "GetFolderPermissions",
        "deprecated": true,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "folderId",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "woC32em2Fb0"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "",
            "headers": {},
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FolderPermissionsResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Folders"
        ],
        "summary": "Add a New Folder Permission",
        "description": "This API allows to create a new folder Permission for users/groups. If any permissions exist for any users/group, they are removed (reset) and permissions provided in Request body are applied.\nIt can also be used to reset the default permission.\nIt takes optional cascade field to add permissions on subfolders recursively.\nYou can specify the versionId in the If-Match header to validate you are working off the latest version of the folder.\n\nThis API takes a default permission, propagation flag and a list of Permissions.\nEach permission has following fields:\n\n- id (id of User or Group)\n\n- type\n\n- permission\n\nThe API also supports **If-Match** optional header to provide the versionId, so you can verify you are working on the latest version. (applicable for single file upload, ignored for multiple file upload)\n\nIf versionId provided in the **If-Match** header is not latest, error Response wiith Response code **412** will be send back to the caller with **Errorcode** INVALID_HEADER &\n**Error Message**: If-Match header value is not latest versionId.\n\nIf the **If-Match** header value is *  or header not provided, actions will be performed on the latest version.\nInheritance flag will be set to false by default.",
        "operationId": "AddaNewFolderPermission",
        "deprecated": true,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "folderId",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "woC32em2Fb0"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "If-Match",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "description": "",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FolderPermissionRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "",
            "headers": {},
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FolderPermissionsResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "tags": [
          "Folders"
        ],
        "summary": "Update existing Folder Permission",
        "description": "This API allows to update existing folder Permissions or add permissions for new users/groups. It can also be used to reset the default permission.\nIt takes optional cascade field to update permissions on subfolders recursively.\nYou can specify the versionId in the If-Match header to validate you are working off the latest version of the folder.\nThis API takes default permission, propagation flag and a list of Permissions.\nEach permission has following fields:\n\n- id (id of User or Group)\n\n- type\n\n- permission\n\nThe API also supports **If-Match** optional header to provide the versionId, so you can verify you are working on the latest version. (applicable for single file upload, ignored for multiple file upload)\n\nIf versionId provided in the **If-Match** header is not latest, error Response wiith Response code **412** will be send back to the caller with **Errorcode** INVALID_HEADER &\n**Error Message**: If-Match header value is not latest versionId.\n\nIf the **If-Match** header value is *  or header not provided, actions will be performed on the latest version.\nInheritance flag will be set to false by default.",
        "operationId": "UpdateexistingFolderPermission",
        "deprecated": true,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "folderId",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "woC32em2Fb0"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "If-Match",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "description": "",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FolderPermissionRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "",
            "headers": {},
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FolderPermissionsResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "tags": [
          "Folders"
        ],
        "summary": "Remove any existing Folder Permission",
        "description": "This API allows to removes specified given permission to given user/group and recomputes permission for actor based on user roles and default permission.\nIt takes optional cascade field to delete permissions on subfolders recursively.\nYou can specify the versionId in the If-Match header to validate you are working off the latest version of the folder.\n\nThis API takes propagation flag and a list of Permissions as a Request Body, each permission has following fields\n\n- id (id of User or Group)\n\n- type\n\nExample : <br/>\n{<br/>\n  \"cascade\": \"true\",<br/>\n  \"permissions\": [<br/>\n    {<br/>\n      \"id\": \"0Z-OMo67VtY\",<br/>\n      \"type\": \"USER\"<br/>\n    },<br/>\n    {<br/>\n      \"id\": \"swO2L9AqeT0\",<br/>\n      \"type\": \"GROUP\"<br/>\n    }<br/>\n  ]<br/>\n}<br/>\nThe API also supports **If-Match** optional header to provide the versionId, so you can verify you are working on the latest version. (applicable for single file upload, ignored for multiple file upload)\n\nIf versionId provided in the **If-Match** header is not latest, error Response wiith Response code **412** will be send back to the caller with **Errorcode** INVALID_HEADER &\n**Error Message**: If-Match header value is not latest versionId.\n\nIf the **If-Match** header value is *  or header not provided, actions will be performed on the latest version.",
        "operationId": "RemoveanyexistingFolderPermission",
        "deprecated": true,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "folderId",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "woC32em2Fb0"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "If-Match",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "",
            "headers": {}
          }
        }
      }
    },
